---
/**
 * /about-us/ `#team` — the centred intro and the four-tier support-staff
 * roster (Patient Coordination → Dental Hygienists → Dental Assistants →
 * Comfort Officers) of paper portrait cards on the sage-pale band.
 *
 * A code_section band, registered as `about_us_team` in
 * src/blocks/CodeSectionBlock.astro. The template hard-codes `id="team"`
 * (about-us/index.astro:601), so `id` defaults to that and CodeSectionBlock
 * overrides it with the row's deduped anchor when one is typed. The four
 * tier ids (coordination / hygienists / assistants / comfort) stay inside the
 * component, as they stay inside the template.
 *
 * ── D1: a route-scoped band reads its own page ────────────────────────────
 * THE TEAM TAB IS THE ONE PEOPLE-LIST ON THE SITE and it is already editable:
 * `team` (nine rows live) is the Team tab under Pages -> About Us, and the
 * intro is the `team-intro` Section-copy row. A code band receives props
 * only, so freezing nine people into the BANDS entry would undo the tab —
 * the plan calls that mandatory (plan-phases Phase 2, dependsOn D1). This
 * component therefore calls `getPageContent(Astro.url.pathname)` itself —
 * the read the template runs at about-us/index.astro:49 — guarded by the
 * `route` prop: on any other route it renders NOTHING and warns, because the
 * rows and the ten image slots it asks for exist only on the About page
 * entry. Decision D1, 2026-09-08 (TrustStrip.astro is the first instance of
 * the pattern).
 *
 * ── What moved here, and what the template keeps ──────────────────────────
 * The roster logic is a COPY of about-us/index.astro:244-354 — TEAM_TIERS
 * (:285-290), cmsTeam / teamGroups (:292-312), TEMPLATE_TEAM_LEDE, countWord
 * and teamLedeFor (:332-344), teamDogs / teamLede (:346-347), and the
 * `teamIntro` introFrom() call (:354) with its literal fallbacks — plus the
 * literal roster `templateTeamGroups` (:147-242), which reads the ten team
 * image slots teamSara … teamBirdie and is the rollback when the Team tab is
 * empty. Here the literal is wrapped in a function that takes `image`,
 * because the read only happens on-route; every name, role, bio, slot and
 * alt is the template's, in the template's order. The template keeps its own
 * copy of all of it for the un-migrated branch (non-negotiable 6) — nothing
 * was deleted there.
 *
 * ── Markup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Verbatim from about-us/index.astro:601-650: `section.section.dark#team` >
 * `.wrap[data-vs-reveal-batch]` > <SectionIntro centered
 * class="aus-section-head"> (eyebrow / heading / headingItalic / lede from
 * teamIntro) + one `div.aus-team-group#<tier>` per tier that has members:
 * `h3.aus-team-group-title` ("{titleStart} <em>{titleAccent}</em>") and
 * `div.aus-team-grid.aus-team-grid-<n>[data-vs-reveal-batch]` (the inner
 * batch staggers the cards independently of the outer one, mirroring the
 * .creds-grid pattern) of `article.aus-team-card` > `.aus-team-pic` > <Image
 * widths=[360,540,720] sizes="(min-width: 1100px) 380px, (min-width: 780px)
 * 50vw, 100vw" loading="lazy" decoding="async"> + `.aus-team-body` >
 * `span.aus-team-role` + h4 + p. data-vs-reveal-batch stays on `.wrap`, as
 * the template has it — not on the section. The lines are copied, not
 * retyped.
 *
 * ONE MEASURED WHITESPACE FACT. The band sits in a ROOT-LEVEL expression
 * (`{onRoute && (…)}`), and @astrojs/compiler 3.0.1 in compact mode drops
 * every whitespace-only text node inside a root-level expression instead of
 * collapsing it to one space as it does under an element (the template's
 * band sits under <main>). Between elements that is invisible — the same
 * residue TrustStrip, HomeTechnologyBand and every Wave B band ship. Inside
 * the tier title it is not: the template's `{group.titleStart} <em>` loses
 * its literal space and would ship "Patient<em>Coordination</em>", so the
 * space travels inside the expression — `{`${group.titleStart} `}<em>` —
 * and ships "Patient <em>Coordination</em>", the template's words. No
 * zero-byte construction restores the element-context behaviour (a leading
 * <style>, <slot />, <Fragment />, comment or expression does not; only a
 * real sibling element does, and a wrapper is exactly what CodeSectionBlock
 * forbids). Compiled with `transform(..., { compact: true })`, the call
 * astro/dist/core/compile/compile.js:19 makes.
 *
 * ── CSS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * about-us.css restated below: `.section` padding (:103, :469), the
 * `.section.dark` band and its ink overrides (:121-132), `.aus-section-head`
 * (:136), the whole TEAM block (:239-345), the 1100px team rules (:453-462)
 * and the 780px rules (:466, :475-486). The page primitives the band's own
 * elements sit on — `.wrap` (:32), the h3/h4 base (:34-37, :41-42), `p`
 * (:43) and `em` (:44) — are folded into the team rules so the box is whole
 * without the page sheet. Astro scopes by attribute, so a bare
 * `.aus-team-card` would tie the page sheet's `.aus .aus-team-card` at
 * (0,2,0) and leave bundle order to decide (CodeSectionBlock.astro, the
 * "Why there is no <style> block" note; TrustBand.astro's <style> header);
 * everything below is rooted at `.section`, and the section rule itself is
 * written `section.section.dark` so it outranks `.aus .section.dark` rather
 * than tying it.
 *
 * The SectionIntro's children (`.aus-section-head`, `.vs-eyebrow`, `h2.vs-h2`,
 * `em.vs-italic-word`, `p.vs-lede`) are rendered by another component and
 * carry no scope attribute, so their page-sheet rules are written through
 * `:global()` under `section.section.dark` — the same reason
 * HomeTechnologyBand writes `.tech h2 :global(em)`. Their site-wide base
 * (global.css:489-497 .vs-h2, :518-524 .vs-lede, :535-538 .vs-italic-word,
 * :546-560 .vs-eyebrow, :647-654 .vs-intro-triad) is BaseLayout's, not the
 * page's, and is not restated. The page sheet's `.aus` aliases (about-us.css
 * :10-29) map 1:1 to `--vs-*` tokens and the token names are used here —
 * with ONE exception: `--shadow` (:21) is a raw value on `.aus`, NOT an alias
 * of `--vs-shadow`, so the card's hover shadow is written out literally.
 * Same computed values either way.
 */
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import SectionIntro from "./SectionIntro.astro";
import { getPageContent, introFrom, type PageContent, type PageImage } from "../lib/page-content";

interface Props {
  /**
   * The route this band belongs to ("/about-us/"). It reads that page's
   * Team tab, `team-intro` Section-copy row and ten team image slots, so on
   * any other route it renders nothing and warns.
   */
  route: string;
  /** The DOM id. CodeSectionBlock overrides it with the row's deduped anchor. */
  id?: string;
}

const { route, id = "team" } = Astro.props;

// trailingSlash is 'always' (astro.config.mjs:21); normalise both sides anyway
// so "/about-us" and "/about-us/" name the same page, as page-content.ts does.
const withSlash = (p: string) => (p.endsWith("/") ? p : `${p}/`);
const here = Astro.url.pathname;
const onRoute = withSlash(here) === withSlash(route);

if (!onRoute) {
  console.warn(
    `[blocks] TeamBand is scoped to ${route} and was asked to render on ${here} — it reads that page's Team tab, "team-intro" section and team image slots, so it renders nothing here`,
  );
}

// about-us/index.astro:279-283 — named "roster" so they cannot be mistaken
// for the loader's TeamMember / TeamPhoto / TeamGroup, which describe a CMS
// row; these describe a card.
type RosterPhoto = Pick<PageImage, 'url' | 'width' | 'height'>;
type RosterMember = { name: string; role: string; bio: string; image: RosterPhoto; alt: string };
type RosterTier = { id: string; titleStart: string; titleAccent: string; members: RosterMember[] };

// about-us/index.astro:147-242 — the literal roster, THE ROLLBACK PATH when
// the Team tab is empty. 4 tier groups, ordered front-office → hygienists →
// assistants → comfort (the order patients meet the team in real life:
// phone/check-in first, then chair-side). The 3 → 2 → 3 → 2 column cadence
// also gives the section a deliberate visual rhythm. Wrapped in a function
// because `image` exists only on-route; the members are the template's,
// character for character.
function templateTeamGroupsFor(image: PageContent["image"]): RosterTier[] {
  return [
    {
      id: 'coordination',
      titleStart: 'Patient',
      titleAccent: 'Coordination',
      members: [
        {
          name: 'Sara',
          role: 'Office Manager',
          bio: "Bachelor's and master's in Healthcare Administration. Sets the tone of the practice and keeps every smile journey moving from first call to final visit.",
          image: image("teamSara"),
          alt: 'Sara, Office Manager at Vivid Smiles',
        },
        {
          name: 'KT',
          role: 'Patient Care & Office Coordinator',
          bio: "Often the first friendly voice you'll hear. Ten years in healthcare and dentistry, recently transplanted to Parker from Colorado's Western Slope.",
          image: image("teamKt"),
          alt: 'KT, Patient Care and Office Coordinator at Vivid Smiles',
        },
        {
          name: 'Carol',
          role: 'Patient Coordinator',
          bio: 'In dentistry since age 19. A Colorado native who hikes with her family and disappears to warm beaches whenever she gets the chance.',
          image: image("teamCarol"),
          alt: 'Carol, Patient Coordinator at Vivid Smiles',
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'hygienists',
      titleStart: 'Dental',
      titleAccent: 'Hygienists',
      members: [
        {
          name: 'Mandy',
          role: 'Registered Dental Hygienist',
          bio: 'A Registered Dental Hygienist since 2011 who grew up in a military family — bringing warm, welcoming energy to every appointment.',
          image: image("teamMandy"),
          alt: 'Mandy, Registered Dental Hygienist at Vivid Smiles',
        },
        {
          name: 'Sammie',
          role: 'Registered Dental Hygienist',
          bio: 'UMKC graduate with seventeen years of hygiene experience and a focus on patient education and personalized oral health care.',
          image: image("teamSammie"),
          alt: 'Sammie, Registered Dental Hygienist at Vivid Smiles',
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'assistants',
      titleStart: 'Dental',
      titleAccent: 'Assistants',
      members: [
        {
          name: 'Linh',
          role: 'Dental Assistant',
          bio: 'Skilled clinical support and patient education, ensuring every visit moves smoothly and every patient feels comfortable.',
          image: image("teamLinh"),
          alt: 'Linh, Dental Assistant at Vivid Smiles',
        },
        {
          name: 'Tina',
          role: 'Expanded Duties Dental Assistant',
          bio: 'An EDDA for nearly twenty years across every dental specialty, with deep experience in surgical work — and a side life of camping, fishing, and four-wheeling.',
          image: image("teamTina"),
          alt: 'Tina, Expanded Duties Dental Assistant at Vivid Smiles',
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: 'comfort',
      titleStart: 'Comfort',
      titleAccent: 'Officers',
      members: [
        {
          name: 'Knox',
          role: 'Director of Smiles',
          bio: 'Part of the practice family since puppyhood. Greets patients with a wagging tail and brightens every visit, one nuzzle at a time.',
          image: image("teamKnox"),
          alt: 'Knox, the Vivid Smiles dog and Director of Smiles',
        },
        {
          name: 'Birdie',
          role: 'Chief Comfort Officer',
          bio: 'Three-legged, rescued from Turkey through Tattered Paws & Golden Hearts. Uncannily good at finding patients who need an extra dose of comfort.',
          image: image("teamBirdie"),
          alt: 'Birdie, the Vivid Smiles dog and Chief Comfort Officer',
        },
      ],
    },
  ];
}

/**
 * ---------- TEAM from WordPress (Pages -> About Us -> Team tab) ----------
 * about-us/index.astro:244-312, copied.
 *
 * A row arrives as getPageContent() shapes it (src/lib/page-content.ts,
 * TeamMember): `name`, `role`, `bio` and `photoAlt` as trimmed text; `group`
 * already unwrapped from the one-element array WPGraphQL sends for every ACF
 * select to a plain id; and `photo` as the same {url, width, height} the
 * Images tab produces — one placeImage() in src/loaders/pages.ts, so a given
 * attachment builds to the same hashed asset whichever tab it was chosen
 * from. A photo is always there: a member without one fails the build in the
 * loader with a message naming the person and the box to fix, so this
 * component never has to draw a card with no picture.
 *
 * The four tiers are fixed here, not in the CMS. An editor picks a tier per
 * person from a select whose four values are exactly the ids below
 * (vs-content-model.php, field_vs_team_group); the tier's heading, its
 * accent word, its anchor id and the order the tiers appear in are design,
 * so they stay in code. A tier nobody is in is not drawn at all — no orphan
 * heading over an empty grid. Every select value has a branch: an id this
 * table does not name cannot be chosen, because the select allows no null
 * and offers nothing else.
 *
 * The grid class is derived from the member count (`aus-team-grid-${n}`), so
 * a count the hand-written roster never produced needs a rule in <style>
 * below or the tier collapses to one column. 1 and 4–6 have their own rules
 * there; larger counts fall to a low-specificity default.
 */
const TEAM_TIERS: Array<Pick<RosterTier, 'id' | 'titleStart' | 'titleAccent'>> = [
  { id: 'coordination', titleStart: 'Patient', titleAccent: 'Coordination' },
  { id: 'hygienists', titleStart: 'Dental', titleAccent: 'Hygienists' },
  { id: 'assistants', titleStart: 'Dental', titleAccent: 'Assistants' },
  { id: 'comfort', titleStart: 'Comfort', titleAccent: 'Officers' },
];

/**
 * about-us/index.astro:314-344, copied. The lede counts the room, and with
 * the CMS list in play it is rebuilt from the rows so that "seven teammates"
 * cannot go stale the day an eighth is added: H is every row outside the
 * comfort tier, D is the comfort tier.
 *
 * PROOF it reproduces today's words. The nine literal cards are 7 humans and
 * 2 dogs; countWord(7) is "seven", countWord(2) is "two", D is not 1 so
 * "dogs", and three clauses take the serial-comma join — giving
 *   "Two doctors, seven teammates, and two very good dogs — hand-picked …"
 * which is TEMPLATE_TEAM_LEDE character for character, including the U+2014
 * dash.
 *
 * One to twelve are spelled out, the way the lede has always spelled "seven"
 * and "two"; beyond that the digits stand. A count of zero drops its clause
 * instead of reading "zero very good dogs", and the join degrades to
 * "Two doctors and seven teammates".
 */
const TEMPLATE_TEAM_LEDE =
  'Two doctors, seven teammates, and two very good dogs — hand-picked for skill, for warmth, and for the quiet way they turn a long appointment into a short one.';

const COUNT_WORDS = ['', 'one', 'two', 'three', 'four', 'five', 'six', 'seven', 'eight', 'nine', 'ten', 'eleven', 'twelve'];
const countWord = (n: number): string => COUNT_WORDS[n] || String(n);

function teamLedeFor(humans: number, dogs: number): string {
  const who = ['Two doctors'];
  if (humans > 0) who.push(`${countWord(humans)} ${humans === 1 ? 'teammate' : 'teammates'}`);
  if (dogs > 0) who.push(`${countWord(dogs)} very good ${dogs === 1 ? 'dog' : 'dogs'}`);
  const list = who.length === 3 ? `${who[0]}, ${who[1]}, and ${who[2]}` : who.join(' and ');
  return `${list} — hand-picked for skill, for warmth, and for the quiet way they turn a long appointment into a short one.`;
}

type Intro = { eyebrow: string; heading: string; headingItalic: string; lede: string };

// about-us/index.astro:49 — the same read the template runs, only on this
// route. Off-route both stay empty and nothing renders.
let teamGroups: RosterTier[] = [];
let teamIntro: Intro = { eyebrow: "", heading: "", headingItalic: "", lede: "" };
if (onRoute) {
  const { section, image, team } = await getPageContent(here);

  // about-us/index.astro:292-312
  const cmsTeam = team.length > 0;

  teamGroups = cmsTeam
    ? TEAM_TIERS.flatMap((tier) => {
        const members = team
          .filter((row) => row.group === tier.id)
          .map((row) => ({
            name: row.name,
            role: row.role,
            bio: row.bio,
            image: row.photo,
            // The Photo description box wins when typed; otherwise the alt is
            // written the way every literal card's alt already reads. The
            // loader resolves the same words into photo.alt (teamPhotoAlt in
            // src/loaders/pages.ts).
            alt: row.photo.alt,
          }));
        return members.length > 0 ? [{ ...tier, members }] : [];
      })
    : templateTeamGroupsFor(image);

  // about-us/index.astro:346-347
  const teamDogs = team.filter((row) => row.group === 'comfort').length;
  const teamLede = cmsTeam ? teamLedeFor(team.length - teamDogs, teamDogs) : TEMPLATE_TEAM_LEDE;

  // about-us/index.astro:354 — the row with the template literal as fallback
  // (page-content.ts introFrom), so the band is byte-identical until the row
  // is filled in wp-admin. team-intro.body is EMPTY live, so the computed
  // lede is what ships.
  teamIntro = introFrom(section("team-intro"), { eyebrow: "The team", heading: "The people who make", headingItalic: "every visit feel easy.", lede: teamLede });
}
---

{
  onRoute && (
      <section class="section dark" id={id}>
        <div class="wrap" data-vs-reveal-batch>
          <SectionIntro
            eyebrow={teamIntro.eyebrow}
            heading={teamIntro.heading}
            headingItalic={teamIntro.headingItalic}
            lede={teamIntro.lede}
            centered
            class="aus-section-head"
          />

          {
            teamGroups.map((group) => (
              <div class="aus-team-group" id={group.id}>
                <h3 class="aus-team-group-title">
                  {`${group.titleStart} `}<em>{group.titleAccent}</em>
                </h3>
                {/* Inner data-vs-reveal-batch staggers the cards independently of the
                  outer wrapper batch, mirroring the .creds-grid pattern. */}
                <div
                  class={`aus-team-grid aus-team-grid-${group.members.length}`}
                  data-vs-reveal-batch
                >
                  {group.members.map((m) => (
                    <article class="aus-team-card">
                      <div class="aus-team-pic">
                        <Image
                          src={m.image.url}
                          width={m.image.width}
                          height={m.image.height}
                          alt={m.alt}
                          widths={[360, 540, 720]}
                          sizes="(min-width: 1100px) 380px, (min-width: 780px) 50vw, 100vw"
                          loading="lazy"
                          decoding="async"
                        />
                      </div>
                      <div class="aus-team-body">
                        <span class="aus-team-role">{m.role}</span>
                        <h4>{m.name}</h4>
                        <p>{m.bio}</p>
                      </div>
                    </article>
                  ))}
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>
  )
}

<style>
  /* ── The band (about-us.css:103, :121) ─────────────────────────────────
     `section.section.dark` rather than `.section.dark` so the scoped rule is
     (0,3,1) against the page sheet's `.aus .section.dark` (0,3,0) — a win,
     not a tie. Values are the same either way. */
  section.section.dark {
    padding: 110px 0;
    background: var(--vs-sage-pale);
    color: var(--vs-ink);
  }
  /* about-us.css:32 */
  .section .wrap { max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 40px; }

  /* ── The SectionIntro's children, through :global() ───────────────────
     They are rendered by SectionIntro/Eyebrow and carry no scope attribute.
     Rooted at `section.section.dark` so each is (0,3,1)+ against the page
     sheet's (0,2,0)–(0,4,0) equivalents. */
  /* about-us.css:136 */
  .section :global(.aus-section-head) { margin: 0 auto 64px; max-width: 760px; }
  /* about-us.css:34-37 + :40 (h2 base), :122-124 and :495 (ink) */
  section.section.dark :global(h2) {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.2vw, 54px);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--vs-ink);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
  }
  /* about-us.css:41 and :44 (italic, weight 300), :126-127 (sage on this band) */
  section.section.dark :global(h2 em) {
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--vs-sage);
  }
  /* about-us.css:43 and :128 — the lede (p.vs-lede) and every p on the band */
  section.section.dark :global(p) { margin: 0; color: var(--vs-ink-soft); }
  /* about-us.css:130-132 — the centred eyebrow reads ink-soft on sage-pale,
     hairlines included. */
  section.section.dark :global(.vs-eyebrow) { color: var(--vs-ink-soft); }
  section.section.dark :global(.vs-eyebrow)::before,
  section.section.dark :global(.vs-eyebrow)::after { background: var(--vs-ink-soft); }

  /* ── TEAM (about-us.css:239-345) ──────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* about-us.css:244-245 */
  .section .aus-team-group { margin-bottom: 90px; }
  .section .aus-team-group:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  /* about-us.css:246-255, over the h3 base at :34-37 and :41 */
  .section .aus-team-group-title {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(24px, 2.4vw, 30px);
    font-weight: 400; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--vs-ink);
    margin: 0 0 38px;
    padding-bottom: 18px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
  }
  /* about-us.css:256-259, over the em base at :44 and :126-127 */
  .section .aus-team-group-title em {
    font-style: italic; font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--vs-sage);
  }

  /* about-us.css:261-269 — per-tier column count: 3-member tiers use a normal
     3-col grid; 2-member tiers (Hygienists, Comfort Officers) use a 2-col grid
     capped at ~880px so the row reads as full instead of leaving a glaring
     empty third cell. */
  .section .aus-team-grid { display: grid; gap: 30px; }
  .section .aus-team-grid-3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  .section .aus-team-grid-2 {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    max-width: 880px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  /* about-us.css:271-293 — counts the CMS can produce that the hand-written
     roster never did. The class is derived from the member count above
     (`aus-team-grid-${group.members.length}`), so every count an editor can
     reach needs a rule here or the tier collapses to one enormous column.
       1      a single card, centred and capped so it reads as a portrait
              rather than a banner (440px ≈ one cell of the 3-col grid).
       4      one row of four; the 4/5 portrait still reads at ~270px.
       5, 6   three across, wrapping.
       7+     the :where() rule. Its specificity stays below every per-count
              rule in this block, so it only ever fills a gap and can never
              override the -2/-3 rules above — and the same holds inside the
              breakpoints below, where the per-count rules are restated. */
  .section .aus-team-grid-1 {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    max-width: 440px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .section .aus-team-grid-4 { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
  .section .aus-team-grid-5,
  .section .aus-team-grid-6 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  .section :where(.aus-team-grid) { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }

  /* about-us.css:295-311 */
  .section .aus-team-card {
    background: var(--vs-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--vs-line);
    border-radius: var(--vs-r-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease, border-color 0.3s ease;
  }
  .section .aus-team-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    /* `--shadow` on `.aus` (about-us.css:21), written out: it is not --vs-shadow. */
    box-shadow: 0 24px 60px -30px rgba(40, 40, 30, 0.25), 0 8px 20px -10px rgba(40, 40, 30, 0.08);
    border-color: rgba(107, 122, 84, 0.32);
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .section .aus-team-card { transition: none; }
    .section .aus-team-card:hover { transform: none; }
  }

  /* about-us.css:313-321 */
  .section .aus-team-pic {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    background: var(--vs-cream);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .section .aus-team-pic img {
    width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block;
  }

